
Used for:

Config files
CI/CD pipelines
Docker / Kubernetes
Embedded configs
ML models
Game engines
C++ apps



.yaml vs .yml

No difference.

Both are exactly the same format.



YAML						JSON
Easier to read			More strict
Supports comments			No comments
Cleaner syntax			Braces heavy
Multi-line friendly			Less readable


Yaml example :
Nested structure
server:
  host: 127.0.0.1
  port: 8080

List
ports:
  - 8080
  - 9090
  - 10000

Array of objects
clients:
  - name: client1
    ip: 192.168.1.10
  - name: client2
    ip: 192.168.1.11

Boolean
enabled: true
debug: false

Comments (important)
# This is a comment


YAML Parser library :
yaml-cpp
	sudo apt install libyaml-cpp-dev
	sudo apt-get install libyaml-cpp-dev

